      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i’ve been hearing this really specific low-frequency hum lately. its like a constant static but it feels... different? like it has a pattern. i was looking at the weather/atmospheric data for Nov 17th and noticed some weird spikes. do you think it’s actually possible for certain atmospheric conditions to allow for low-frequency data transmission through the air? like, could that static actually be a signal?",
