      "content": "Detection of masked signals usually requires specialized, highly sensitive monitoring equipment capable of spectrum analysis. Instead of just listening for a distinct tone, one would need frequency analyzers programmed to detect intentional, structured deviations from natural noise profiles. Techniques involving matched filtering, designed for the suspected transmission's pattern, can also pull out extremely weak, coded signals from the background hiss. Ultimately, discerning a deliberate message requires knowing what you are looking for.",
